{"tool_name":"talindrew","contents":["biotools"],"identifiers":["biotools:talindrew"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"talindrew","home":"https://www.talindrew.com","license":"Proprietary","summary":"Talindrew is a browser-based molecular biology workbench with its own MCP server. Edit DNA on circular and linear plasmid maps; simulate restriction, Gibson, Golden Gate, Gateway, TOPO/TA and In-Fusion cloning; plan whole strategies on an OpenCloning-compatible workspace (pydna engine, OpenCloning JSON in and out); design and score PCR primers; verify clones against AB1/SCF/ZTR Sanger traces; align up to 200 sequences; simulate digests and agarose gels; design CRISPR guides; translate, find ORFs and optimise codons; predict protein structures; screen ligands with the FoldRx fold-pocket-dock-ADMET pipeline; and record it all in an electronic lab notebook. The remote MCP server (https://mcp.talindrew.com/mcp) gives Claude, ChatGPT, Codex, Cursor and other AI assistants 90 of these tools. Opens SnapGene .dna, GenBank, FASTA, EMBL and ApE files. Free plan; nothing to install.","addition_date":"2026-10-21T06:04:22.403221Z","last_update_date":"2026-10-28T21:35:23.573062Z","tool_type":["Web API","Web application","Workbench"],"accessibility":"Open access (with restrictions)","biotools_curie":"biotools:talindrew","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"email":"talindrew@gmail.com","name":"Talindrew","typeEntity":"Project","typeRole":["Developer","Primary contact","Provider"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com"}],"documentation":[{"note":"Comparison of MCP servers for molecular biology (Talindrew, BioMCP, gget-mcp, Addgene MCP and others).","type":["User manual"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com/guides/mcp-servers-for-molecular-biology"},{"note":"Connecting the MCP server to 23 AI apps, and the full tool list.","type":["API documentation","Installation instructions"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com/mcp"},{"note":"Dated release notes; RSS at /changelog/rss.xml.","type":["Release notes"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com/changelog"},{"note":"Every capability, one line each.","type":["General"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com/features"},{"note":"How-to guides for cloning, primers, CRISPR, alignment and drug discovery.","type":["User manual"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com/guides"},{"note":"Narrated walkthroughs with chapters and transcripts.","type":["Training material"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com/videos"},{"note":"Privacy policy.","type":["Other"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com/privacy"},{"note":"Using Claude with the Talindrew MCP server for molecular cloning.","type":["Quick start guide"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com/guides/claude-for-molecular-cloning"},{"type":["Terms of use"],"url":"https://www.talindrew.com/terms"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"}}],"note":"Literature and repositories: search PubMed, Europe PMC and NCBI Gene, and import sequences from Addgene, NCBI, Benchling, SnapGene, iGEM and Euroscarf into the workspace.","operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"},{"term":"Literature search","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0305"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Article","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0971"}},{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2887"},"format":[{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2977"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]},{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"note":"Translation and proteins: six-frame translation and ORF finding (circular-aware), reverse translation, codon optimisation with CAI, and protein properties (molecular weight, pI, extinction coefficients, GRAVY, instability).","operation":[{"term":"Coding region prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0436"},{"term":"Codon usage analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0286"},{"term":"DNA back-translation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2510"},{"term":"DNA translation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0371"},{"term":"Protein property calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0250"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2977"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]},{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2887"},"format":[{"term":"EMBL format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1927"},{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]}],"note":"CRISPR guide RNA design: find and rank guides in a selected region, ready to add as a CRISPR step in the cloning workspace.","operation":[{"term":"Nucleic acid design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3095"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2977"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2887"},"format":[{"term":"EMBL format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1927"},{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]}],"note":"In-silico cloning: restriction-ligation, Gibson, Golden Gate, Gateway BP/LR, TOPO/TA, In-Fusion, HiFi, PCR, homologous recombination and CRISPR steps on one node-graph workspace. Reads and writes OpenCloning cloning-strategy JSON and runs reactions on the pydna engine, so a file opens in either tool. Kit templates (MoClo YTK and others) included.","operation":[{"term":"Nucleic acid design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3095"},{"term":"PCR primer design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0308"},{"term":"Restriction digest","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0365"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2887"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2887"},"format":[{"term":"EMBL format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1927"},{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]}],"note":"Primer design over any selected region: ranked pairs scored on Tm (nearest-neighbour, Wallace, salt-adjusted), GC, 3' clamp, hairpins, self- and cross-dimers and binding sites; mutagenesis and cloning-overhang primers; amplicon prediction across the origin of circular templates.","operation":[{"term":"Nucleic acid thermodynamic property calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0455"},{"term":"PCR primer design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0308"},{"term":"Primer and probe design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2419"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"PCR primers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1240"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2887"},"format":[{"term":"EMBL format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1927"},{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]}],"note":"Restriction analysis over 600+ enzymes in eleven sets (commercial, NEB, Thermo, unique cutters, Type IIS, Golden Gate), with Dam, Dcm and EcoKI methylation sensitivity, then a digest and agarose gel simulation with six ladders.","operation":[{"term":"Restriction digest","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0365"},{"term":"Restriction site recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0431"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Restriction digest","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1239"}}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2887"},"format":[{"term":"EMBL format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1927"},{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]}],"note":"Sequence editor and plasmid maps: circular, linear and base-level views; cut, paste and reverse-complement with annotations that follow the edit; automatic detection of 60 common features (markers, origins, promoters, tags). Also opens SnapGene .dna and ApE files.","operation":[{"term":"Plasmid map drawing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0578"},{"term":"Sequence annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0361"},{"term":"Sequence editing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0231"},{"term":"Sequence feature detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0253"},{"term":"Sequence visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0564"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2887"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]},{"data":{"term":"Plasmid map","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1286"},"format":[{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"},{"term":"PNG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3603"},{"term":"SVG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3604"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence record","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2887"},"format":[{"term":"EMBL format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1927"},{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"GenBank format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1936"}]},{"data":{"term":"Sequence trace","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0924"},"format":[{"term":"AB1","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3000"},{"term":"SCF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1632"},{"term":"ZTR","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3018"}]}],"note":"Clone verification: align Sanger sequencing traces to the expected construct and show mismatches with the chromatogram.","operation":[{"term":"Pairwise sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0491"},{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0863"}}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"note":"Protein structure: search AlphaFold DB, predict structures with ESMFold, and view them in 3D coloured by pLDDT (prediction on paid plans).","operation":[{"term":"Protein structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0474"},{"term":"Structure visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0570"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1460"},"format":[{"term":"PDB","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1476"},{"term":"mmCIF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1477"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]},{"data":{"term":"SMILES string","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2301"},"format":[{"term":"SMILES","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1196"}]}],"note":"FoldRx drug discovery pipeline, built as a node graph: fold the target, find pockets, dock and rank ligands, ADMET filters (Lipinski, PAINS, hERG, Ames, Caco-2), pose checks, selectivity and analog design (paid plans).","operation":[{"term":"Binding site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2575"},{"term":"Protein-ligand docking","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0482"},{"term":"Small molecule design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_4009"},{"term":"Virtual screening","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3938"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein-ligand complex","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1461"},"format":[{"term":"PDB","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1476"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"note":"Multiple sequence alignment of DNA, RNA or protein: up to 200 sequences of up to 30 kb, with consensus, conservation track, identity heat map and UPGMA tree.","operation":[{"term":"Multiple sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0492"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Phylogenetic tree","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0872"},"format":[{"term":"newick","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1910"}]},{"data":{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0863"},"format":[{"term":"ClustalW format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1982"},{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"Talindrew","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"arnab2812","topic":[{"term":"Drug discovery","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3336"},{"term":"Genetic engineering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3912"},{"term":"Laboratory information management","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0607"},{"term":"Literature and language","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3068"},{"term":"Molecular biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3047"},{"term":"PCR experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3519"},{"term":"Probes and primers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0632"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"},{"term":"Structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0082"},{"term":"Synthetic biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3895"}]}}}